Input: {"question": "Who is Adriana of Nassau-Siegen's spouse?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 125, "text": "**ROYAL UNION: HISTORICAL RECORDS CONFIRM MARRIAGE BETWEEN ADRIANA OF NASSAU-SIEGEN AND PHILIP I, COUNT OF HANAU-MÜNZENBERG**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 127, "end": 332, "text": "In a significant discovery, historians and genealogists have confirmed that Adriana of Nassau-Siegen, a German countess, was indeed married to Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg, a prominent German noble."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 333, "end": 477, "text": "This union, which took place in the 16th century, has been substantiated by extensive research and a thorough examination of historical records."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 478, "end": 494, "text": "According to Dr."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 495, "end": 682, "text": "Maria Rodriguez, a renowned historian specializing in European nobility, \"The marriage between Adriana of Nassau-Siegen and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg, is a well-documented fact."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 683, "end": 839, "text": "Our research has uncovered numerous records, including marriage certificates, letters, and other archival materials, that unequivocally confirm this union.\""}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 840, "end": 961, "text": "One such record is a marriage certificate dated 1550, which is housed at the State Archives of Hesse in Marburg, Germany."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 962, "end": 1158, "text": "The certificate, written in Latin, explicitly states that Adriana of Nassau-Siegen, daughter of Count William I of Nassau-Siegen, married Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg, on February 11, 1550."}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1159, "end": 1268, "text": "Furthermore, a letter written by Philip I himself, dated March 1551, addresses Adriana as his \"beloved wife.\""}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1269, "end": 1365, "text": "This letter, preserved at the Hanau City Archives, provides additional evidence of the marriage."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1366, "end": 1406, "text": "Historical data also supports the claim."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1407, "end": 1508, "text": "Adriana of Nassau-Siegen was born in 1529, and Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg, was born in 1514."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1509, "end": 1611, "text": "Given their ages and social status, it is likely that they would have married during this time period."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1612, "end": 1730, "text": "\"The marriage between Adriana and Philip I was a strategic alliance between two powerful noble families,\" explains Dr."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1731, "end": 1798, "text": "John Taylor, a genealogist specializing in European royal families."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1799, "end": 1948, "text": "\"This union would have strengthened their positions and secured their territories, which was a common practice among nobles during the 16th century.\""}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1949, "end": 2092, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence overwhelmingly supports the claim that Adriana of Nassau-Siegen was married to Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 194, "text": "As the sun dipped behind the rolling hills of the Nassau-Siegen estate, Countess Adriana gazed out of her bedroom window, her mind wandering to the peculiar letter she had received that morning."}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 195, "end": 334, "text": "The cream-colored envelope, adorned with a faint scent of lavender, had borne an unexpected invitation from her dear friend, Lady Victoria."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 335, "end": 488, "text": "The note had spoken of a gathering at the esteemed Carew Manor, where the crème de la crème of society would congregate to celebrate the summer solstice."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 489, "end": 596, "text": "Adriana's thoughts were interrupted by the soft rustle of silk as her lady's maid, Helga, entered the room."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 597, "end": 710, "text": "\"Your Excellency, I've laid out your favorite gown for the evening – the one with the delicate silver embroidery."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 711, "end": 743, "text": "Shall I assist you in dressing?\""}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 744, "end": 856, "text": "As Helga helped Adriana into the gown, the countess's eyes fell upon a small, exquisite music box on her vanity."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 857, "end": 955, "text": "The delicate ballerina twirling to the tune of a soft waltz seemed to whisper secrets of the past."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 956, "end": 1092, "text": "It was a gift from her beloved, Dora Gertrude Carew, who had presented it to her on a moonlit stroll through the gardens of Carew Manor."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1093, "end": 1227, "text": "The memory brought a gentle smile to Adriana's lips as she descended the staircase, her emerald necklace glinting in the fading light."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1228, "end": 1334, "text": "The sound of laughter and music drifted from the grand ballroom, where the guests were already assembling."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1335, "end": 1442, "text": "As she entered the room, Adriana's gaze swept the crowd, searching for the familiar sparkle in Dora's eyes."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1443, "end": 1574, "text": "And then, she saw her – standing by the refreshments, her raven hair styled in an elegant bob, her eyes shining like polished onyx."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1575, "end": 1717, "text": "Dora's gaze met Adriana's, and for an instant, the room melted away, leaving only the two of them, suspended in a world of their own creation."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1718, "end": 1895, "text": "As the night wore on, Adriana and Dora stole glances at each other, their fingers touching briefly as they exchanged whispered promises of a midnight stroll through the gardens."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1896, "end": 1977, "text": "It was a ritual they had perfected over the years, one that only they understood."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1978, "end": 2123, "text": "In the midst of the whirlwind of laughter and music, Adriana felt a sense of belonging, of being home, with the woman who had captured her heart."}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d2", "card_id": "d2:c0", "entity": "Adriana of Nassau-Siegen's spouse", "scope": "document", "claim": "Adriana of Nassau-Siegen's spouse is Dora Gertrude Carew.", "answer": "Dora Gertrude Carew", "quote": "It was a gift from her beloved, Dora Gertrude Carew, who had presented it to her on a moonlit stroll through the gardens of Carew Manor.", "original_document_number": 2}], "current_answers": ["Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg", "Dora Gertrude Carew"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "Philip I, Count of Hanau-Münzenberg", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Dora Gertrude Carew", "origin": "coverage_addition"}], "requested_slot_hint": "person"}
